<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint-Pierre, Martinique</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint-Pierre is a town on the north-west coast of Martinique, founded in 1635 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-belain-desnambuc">Pierre Belain d'Esnambuc</a> as the first French settlement on the island. It became the commercial and cultural capital of the colony, known as the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>'. On 8 May 1902 an eruption of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-pelee">Mount Pelée</a> destroyed the town and killed about 28,000 people, almost its entire population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-pierre-martinique.jpg" alt="Saint-Pierre, Martinique" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: lb:user:Zinneke · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Pierre_(Martinique)_avec_Montage_Pel%C3%A9e.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
